> I'm trying to post it, but it gives an error "Package Size" and highlights the delivery section that says "Select the package size that best fits your item." But I don't see any way to do that.
**assistant**:
> That usually means eBay requires shipping dimensions/weight, but its listing form has hidden the selector or failed to load it.
> 
> Try:
> 
> 1. In **Delivery**, click **Edit** beside the shipping service/policy (or remove and re-add the shipping option).
> 2. Look for **Package details**, **Package size**, or **Custom package**.
> 3. Choose **Custom package** and enter the packed dimensions and weight—not just the screen itself.
> 4. If you use calculated shipping, package size is mandatory. For flat-rate/free shipping, eBay may still require dimensions depending on the category.
> 
> For a Model Y display, a conservative packed estimate might be:
> - **16 × 12 × 6 in**
> - **5 lb**
> 
> Use your actual box and packing material when possible.
> 
> If no package-size control appears:
> - Save as a draft, reload, and edit the draft.
> - Try eBay’s desktop site in another browser/private window; disable ad/script blockers.
> - Switch temporarily from a shipping policy to manually entered shipping.
> - If using the mobile app, try the browser/desktop listing flow—this is often a UI glitch in the app.
> 
> Do not enter dimensions that are smaller than the eventual box, since carrier adjustments can be charged back to you.
